H4400.definition:
from the same as H4397 (מֲלְאָךְ);
a message
KJV: message.

H4401.definition:
from the same as H4397 (מֲלְאָךְ); ministrative;
Malaki, a prophet
KJV: Malachi.

H4402.definition:
from H4390 (מָלֵא);
fulness, i.e. (concretely) a plump socket (of the eye)
KJV: [idiom] fitly.

H4403.definition:
or מַלְבֻּשׁ; from H3847 (לָבַשׁ);
a garment, or (collectively) clothing
KJV: apparel, raiment, vestment.

H4404.definition:
from H3835 (לָבַן) (denominative);
a brickkiln
KJV: brickkiln.

H4405.definition:
from H4448 (מָלַל) (plural masculine as if from מִלֶּה;
a word; collectively, a discourse; figuratively, a topic
KJV: [phrase] answer, by-word, matter, any thing (what) to say, to speak(-ing), speak, talking, word.

H4406.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4405 (מִלָּה);
a word, command, discourse, or subject
KJV: commandment, matter, thing. word.

H4407.definition:
or מִלֹּא; (2 Kings 12:20), from H4390 (מָלֵא);
a rampart (as filled in), i.e. the citadel
KJV: Millo. See also H1037 (בֵּית מִלּוֹא).

H4408.definition:
from H4414 (מָלַח);
sea-purslain (from its saltness)
KJV: mallows.

H4409.definition:
or מַלּוּכִי; (Nehemiah 12:14), from H4427 (מָלַךְ); remnant;
Malluk, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Malluch, Melichu (from the margin).

H4410.definition:
feminine passive participle of H4427 (מָלַךְ);
something ruled, i.e. a realm
KJV: kingsom, king's, [idiom] royal.

H4411.definition:
from H3885 (לוּן);
a lodgment, i.e. caravanserai or encampment
KJV: inn, place where...lodge, lodging (place).

H4412.definition:
feminine from H3885 (לוּן);
a hut, a hammock
KJV: cottage, lodge.

H4415.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4414 (מָלַח);
to eat salt, i.e. (generally) subsist
KJV: [phrase] have maintenance.

H4416.definition:
(Aramaic) from H4415 (מְלַח);
salt
KJV: [phrase] maintenance, salt.

H4417.definition:
from H4414 (מָלַח);
properly, powder, i.e. (specifically) salt (as easily pulverized and dissolved)
KJV: salt(-pit).

H4418.definition:
from H4414 (מָלַח) in its original sense;
a rag or old garment
KJV: rotten rag.

H4419.definition:
from H4414 (מָלַח) in its second. sense;
a sailor (as following 'the salt')
KJV: mariner.

H4420.definition:
from H4414 (מָלַח) (in its denominative sense); understood as land (H776 (אֶרֶץ))
properly, salted (i.e. land), i.e. a desert
KJV: barren land(-ness), salt (land).

H4421.definition:
from H3898 (לָחַם) (in the sense of fighting);
a battle (i.e. the engagement); generally, war (i.e. warfare)
KJV: battle, fight(-ing), war(-rior).

H4422.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be smooth, i.e. (by implication) to escape (as if by slipperiness); causatively, to release or rescue; specifically, to bring forth young, emit sparks
KJV: deliver (self), escape, lay, leap out, let alone, let go, preserve, save, [idiom] speedily, [idiom] surely.

H4423.definition:
from H4422 (מָלַט),
cement (from its plastic smoothness)
KJV: clay.

H4424.definition:
from H4423 (מֶלֶט) and H3050 (יָהּ); (whom) Jah has delivered;
Melatjah, a Gibeonite
KJV: Melatiah.

H4425.definition:
from H4449 (מְלַל) (in the sense of cropping (compare H4135 (מוּל)));
a head of grain (as cut off)
KJV: ear.

H4426.definition:
from H3887 (לוּץ);
an aphorism; also a satire
KJV: interpretation, taunting.

H4427.definition:
a primitive root;
to reign; inceptively, to ascend the throne; causatively, to induct into royalty; hence (by implication) to take counsel
KJV: consult, [idiom] indeed, be (make, set a, set up) king, be (make) queen, (begin to, make to) reign(-ing), rule, [idiom] surely.

H4428.definition:
from H4427 (מָלַךְ);
a king
KJV: king, royal.

H4429.definition:
the same as H4428 (מֶלֶךְ); king;
Melek, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Melech, Hammelech (by including the article).

H4430.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4428 (מֶלֶךְ);
a king
KJV: king, royal.

H4431.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H4427 (מָלַךְ) in the sense of consultation;
advice
KJV: counsel.

H4432.definition:
from H4427 (מָלַךְ);
Molek (i.e. king), the chief deity of the Ammonites
KJV: Molech. Compare H4445 (מַלְכָּם).

H4433.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4436 (מַלְכָּה);
a queen
KJV: queen.

H4434.definition:
from H3920 (לָכַד);
a snare
KJV: trap.

H4435.definition:
a form of H4436 (מַלְכָּה); queen;
Milcah, the name of a Hebrewess and of an Israelite
KJV: Milcah.

H4436.definition:
feminine of H4428 (מֶלֶךְ);
a queen
KJV: queen.

H4437.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4438 (מַלְכוּת);
dominion (abstractly or concretely)
KJV: kingdom, kingly, realm, reign.

H4438.definition:
or מַלְכֻת; or (in plural) מַלְכֻיָּה; from H4427 (מָלַךְ);
a rule; concretely, a dominion
KJV: empire, kingdom, realm, reign, royal.

H4439.definition:
from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) and H410 (אֵל); king of (i.e. appointed by) God;
Malkiel, an Israelite
KJV: Malchiel.

H4440.definition:
patronymical from H4439 (מַלְכִּיאֵל);
a Malkielite or descendant of Malkiel
KJV: Malchielite.

H4441.definition:
or מַלְכִּיָּהוּlemma מַלְכִּיָהוּ missing dagesh, corrected to מַלְכִּיָּהוּ; (Jeremiah [38:6), from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) and H3050 (יָהּ); king of (i.e. appointed by) Jah;
Malkijah, the name of ten Israelites
KJV: Malchiah, Malchijah.

H4442.definition:
from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) and H6664 (צֶדֶק); king of right;
Malki-Tsedek, an early king in Palestine
KJV: Melchizedek.

H4443.definition:
from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) and H7311 (רוּם); king of a high one (i.e. of exaltation);
Malkiram, an Israelite
KJV: Malchiram.

H4444.definition:
from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) and H7769 (שׁוּעַ); king of wealth;
Malkishua, an Israelite
KJV: Malchishua.

H4445.definition:
or מִלְכּוֹם; from H4428 (מֶלֶךְ) for H4432 (מֹלֶךְ);
Malcam or Milcom, the national idol of the Ammonites
KJV: Malcham, Milcom.

H4446.definition:
from H4427 (מָלַךְ);
a queen
KJV: queen.

H4447.definition:
feminine active participle of H4427 (מָלַךְ); queen;
Moleketh, an Israelitess
KJV: Hammoleketh (including the article).

H4448.definition:
a primitive root;
to speak (mostly poetical) or say
KJV: say, speak, utter.

H4449.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4448 (מָלַל);
to speak
KJV: say, speak(-ing).

H4450.definition:
from H4448 (מָלַל); talkative;
Milalai, an Israelite
KJV: Milalai.

H4451.definition:
from H3925 (לָמַד);
a goad for oxen
KJV: goad.

H4452.definition:
a primitive root;
to be smooth, i.e. (figuratively) pleasant
KJV: be sweet.

H4453.definition:
of Persian derivation;
the butler or other officer in the Babylonian court
KJV: Melzar.

H4454.definition:
a primitive root;
to crack a joint; by implication, to wring the neck of afowl (without separating it)
KJV: wring off.

H4455.definition:
from H3947 (לָקַח);
transitively (in dual) the jaws (as taking food); intransitively, spoil (and captives) (as taken)
KJV: booty, jaws, prey.

H4456.definition:
from H3953 (לָקַשׁ); (compare H3954 (לֶקֶשׁ))
the spring rain; figuratively, eloquence
KJV: latter rain.

H4457.definition:
or מַלְקָח; from H3947 (לָקַח);
(only in dual) tweezers
KJV: snuffers, tongs.

H4458.definition:
from an unused root meaning to spread out;
a wardrobe (i.e. room where clothing is spread)
KJV: vestry.

H4459.definition:
transp. for H4973 (מְתַלְּעָה);
a grinder, i.e. back tooth
KJV: great tooth.

H4460.definition:
from H4048 (מָגַר) (in the sense of depositing);
a granary
KJV: barn.

H4461.definition:
from H4058 (מָדַד);
a measure
KJV: measure.

H4462.definition:
or (transp.) מוֹמֻכָן; (Esther 1:16), of Persian derivation;
Memucan or Momucan, a Persian satrap
KJV: Memucan.

H4463.definition:
from H4191 (מוּת);
a mortal disease; concretely, a corpse
KJV: death.

H4464.definition:
from an unused root meaning to alienate;
a mongrel, i.e. born of aJewish father and aheathen mother
KJV: bastard.

H4465.definition:
from H4376 (מָכַר);
merchandise; abstractly, a selling
KJV: [idiom] ought, (that which cometh of) sale, that which...sold, ware.

H4466.definition:
feminine of H4465 (מִמְכָּר);
a sale
KJV: [phrase] sold as.

H4467.definition:
from H4427 (מָלַךְ);
dominion, i.e. (abstractly) the estate (rule) or (concretely) the country (realm)
KJV: kingdom, king's, reign, royal.

H4468.definition:
a form of H4467 (מַמְלָכָה) and equiv. to it
{dominion, i.e. (abstractly) the estate (rule) or (concretely) the country (realm)}
KJV: kingdom, reign.

H4469.definition:
from H4537 (מָסַךְ);
mixture, i.e. (specifically) wine mixed (with water or spices)
KJV: drink-offering, mixed wine.

H4470.definition:
from an unused root meaning to grieve;
sorrow
KJV: bitterness.

H4471.definition:
from H4754 (מָרָא)(in the sense of vigor); lusty;
Mamre, an Amorite
KJV: Mamre.

H4472.definition:
from H4843 (מָרַר);
a bitterness, i.e. (figuratively) calamity
KJV: bitterness.

H4473.definition:
from H4886 (מָשַׁח), in the sense of expansion;
outspread (i.e. with outstretched wings)
KJV: anointed.

H4474.definition:
from H4910 (מָשַׁל);
a ruler or (abstractly) rule
KJV: dominion, that ruled.

H4475.definition:
feminine of H4474 (מִמְשָׁל);
rule; also (concretely in plural) a realm or a ruler
KJV: dominion, government, power, to rule.

H4476.definition:
from the same as H4943 (מֶשֶׁק);
a possession
KJV: breeding.

H4477.definition:
from H4985 (מָתַק);
something sweet (literally or figuratively)
KJV: (most) sweet.

H4478.definition:
from H4100 (מָה);
literally a whatness (so to speak), i.e. manna (so called from the question about it)
KJV: manna.

H4479.definition:
(Aramaic) from H4101 (מָה);
who or what (properly, interrogatively, hence, also indefinitely and relatively)
KJV: what, who(-msoever, [phrase] -so).

H4480.definition:
or מִנִּי; or מִנֵּי; (constructive plural) (Isaiah 30:11); for H4482 (מֵן);
properly, a part of; hence (prepositionally), from or out of in many senses
KJV: above, after, among, at, because of, by (reason of), from (among), in, [idiom] neither, [idiom] nor, (out) of, over, since, [idiom] then, through, [idiom] whether, with.

H4481.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4480 (מִן)
{properly, a part of; hence (prepositionally), from or out of}
KJV: according, after, [phrase] because, [phrase] before, by, for, from, [idiom] him, [idiom] more than, (out) of, part, since, [idiom] these, to, upon, [phrase] when.

H4482.definition:
from an unused root meaning to apportion; a part; hence,
a musical chord (as parted into strings)
KJV: in (the same) (Psalm 68:23), stringed instrument (Psalm 150:4), whereby (Psalm 45:8 (defective plural)).

H4483.definition:
(Aramaic) or מְנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H4487 (מָנָה);
to count, appoint
KJV: number, ordain, set.

H4484.definition:
(Aramaic) passive participle of H4483 (מְנָא);
numbered
KJV: Mene.

H4485.definition:
from H5059 (נָגַן);
a satire
KJV: music.

H4486.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4093 (מַדָּע);
wisdom or intelligence
KJV: knowledge, reason, understanding.

H4487.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to weigh out; by implication, to allot or constitute officially; also to enumerate or enroll
KJV: appoint, count, number, prepare, set, tell.

H4488.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה);
properly, a fixed weight or measured amount, i.e. (techn.) a maneh or mina
KJV: maneh, pound.

H4489.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה);
properly, something weighed out, i.e. (figuratively) a portion of time, i.e. an instance
KJV: time.

H4490.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה);
properly, something weighed out, i.e. (generally) a division; specifically (of food) a ration; also a lot
KJV: such things as belonged, part, portion.

H4491.definition:
from H5090 (נָהַג);
the driving (of a chariot)
KJV: driving.

H4492.definition:
from H5102 (נָהַר);
properly, a channel or fissure, i.e. (by implication) a cavern
KJV: den.

H4493.definition:
from H5110 (נוּד)
a nodding or toss (of the head in derision)
KJV: shaking.

H4494.definition:
from H5117 (נוּחַ);
quiet, i.e. (concretely) a settled spot, or (figuratively) a home
KJV: (place of) rest.

H4495.definition:
the same as H4494 (מָנוֹחַ); rest;
Manoach, an Israelite
KJV: Manoah.

H4496.definition:
or מְנֻחָה; feminine of H4495 (מָנוֹחַ);
repose or (adverbially) peacefully; figuratively, consolation (specifically, matrimony); hence (concretely) an abode
KJV: comfortable, ease, quiet, rest(-ing place), still.

H4497.definition:
from H5125 (נוּן);
a continuator, i.e. heir
KJV: son.

H4498.definition:
from H5127 (נוּס);
a retreat (literally or figuratively); abstractly, a fleeing
KJV: [idiom] apace, escape, way to flee, flight, refuge.

H4499.definition:
or מְנֻסָה; feminine of H4498 (מָנוֹס);
retreat
KJV: fleeing, flight.
